course: dictionary
lesson: 5930
title: Martial: fighting and war
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Martial» is an adjective that means connected with fighting or war. You will mostly meet it in two phrases: «martial arts» and «martial law». The word around it gives you the clues.
explain: «Martial arts» are fighting sports and skills, such as karate, judo, kung fu and taekwondo. The clues are in the sentences: «karate teaches you to avoid fights» and «judo's first lesson is how to fall safely». So martial arts are about control and respect, not just fighting.
explain: «Martial law» is different. It is when the army takes control of a country instead of the usual government. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Martial means connected with fighting or war.
fact: «Martial arts» are fighting sports and skills, such as karate, judo, kung fu and taekwondo.
fact: «Martial law» is when the army takes control of a country instead of the usual government.
fact: Martial arts start with control and respect, and the first rule is to avoid fights.
fact: Judo and other martial arts teach students how to fall safely.
exercise: In «martial arts», what does martial mean? | *Connected with fighting or war | Connected with food | Connected with music | Connected with the sea
exercise: «Martial law» is when the army takes control of a country instead of the usual government. Who is in charge during martial law? | The school council | The local library | *The army | The children in the playground
exercise: In children's martial arts clubs, what is the first rule? | To fight outside the club | To shout the loudest | To win every match | *To avoid fights
test: Judo is a «martial art». What is judo? | *A fighting sport and skill | A king's law | A type of army tent | A kind of music played in war
test: A club may throw out a pupil who uses martial arts to fight outside. Why does the club do this? | *Because it breaks the rule to avoid fights | Because the pupil is too young to read | Because the pupil has a coloured belt | Because the pupil is too tired to train
exam: Which phrase means that the army takes control of a country instead of the usual government? | *Martial law | Martial soup | Martial arts | Martial tennis
